-- title:
--   Two ring homomorphisms of $\mathbb{C}$ agreeing on $K$ and at $u$ agree on all of $K(u)$
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ be a subfield, $u \in \mathbb{C}$, and $K(u) = \operatorname{hull}(K,u)$ the subfield generated by $K$ and $u$. Let $f, g : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}$ be ring homomorphisms with
--
--   $$f|_{K} = g|_{K} \qquad\text{and}\qquad f(u) = g(u).$$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$\forall\, z \in K(u), \qquad f(z) = g(z).$$
--
--   **Why.** The set on which two ring homomorphisms agree is closed under the field operations, hence is a subfield; by hypothesis it contains $K$ and $u$, so it contains the subfield they generate. Formally this is an induction over `Subfield.closure_induction`, one case per operation.
--
--   **Role.** This is the rigidity step of the closure theorem: *a homomorphism is determined by these data*. It is what makes the intertwining of conjugation in the transfer results automatic rather than something that has to be arranged — the two maps $\Phi \circ (\bar{\cdot})$ and $(\bar{\cdot}) \circ \Phi$ agree on the base and at the generator, so they agree on the whole hull.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/carlok/diaz-modulus-lean/blob/801802b8ac052dff50baf17ac4a7ceac3e994ca9/Diaz/Closure.lean#L125-L140

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Diaz_Closure

open ComplexConjugate
open Diaz
variable (K : Subfield ℂ) (u : ℂ)
variable {K u}

theorem Diaz.eqOn_hull (f g : ℂ →+* ℂ) (hK : ∀ z ∈ K, f z = g z) (hu : f u = g u) :
    ∀ z ∈ hull K u, f z = g z := by sorry
